{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>נצב [stands].</b> Therefore 'נצב' is not a noun but a verb form of the heavy [binyan] construction that is expanded [i.e., hitpa'el or nifal with reflexive/passive force]. Its counterpart is לדין [to judge]. The meaning: [He stands] over His decrees." "<b>עמים [peoples].</b> Its sense is plural, like עמים הר יקראו (Deuteronomy 33:19)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:45.675919391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}